1
00:00:01,114 --> 00:00:05,101
Welcome to the Synthograsizer, a suite of creative

2
00:00:05,101 --> 00:00:08,301
tools for turning ideas into prompts,

3
00:00:08,301 --> 00:00:11,841
images, video, agents, and shared live visuals.

4
00:00:11,995 --> 00:00:14,385
Here is a quick tour of what it can do.

5
00:00:19,122 --> 00:00:22,693
The Synthograsizer turns a prompt into an instrument.

6
00:00:22,876 --> 00:00:26,000
Each knob controls a variable, so you can explore

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,938
new combinations without rewriting your idea.

8
00:00:29,358 --> 00:00:33,825
Switch to the D-pad for focused navigation, or browse the built-in

9
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:37,890
library for generative art, characters, stories, and music.

10
00:00:38,255 --> 00:00:40,878
Start with a template, then make it your own.

11
00:00:44,959 --> 00:00:47,172
Prompt Batch turns one template

12
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:49,715
into a whole collection of prompts.

13
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:53,350
For each variable, choose whether to lock it, randomise

14
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:56,762
it, step through its values in order, or repeat them.

15
00:00:57,205 --> 00:01:00,683
Set the batch size and an output format, then generate.

16
00:01:01,245 --> 00:01:05,061
Review the list, copy it all, or download it for another tool.

17
00:01:11,855 --> 00:01:14,499
Start with an idea in plain language.

18
00:01:14,884 --> 00:01:17,635
Here, a retro-futurist greenhouse becomes

19
00:01:17,635 --> 00:01:20,454
a reusable template, with separate controls

20
00:01:20,454 --> 00:01:23,649
for architecture, plants, lighting, and colour.

21
00:01:23,852 --> 00:01:26,308
Choose a model, generate the template,

22
00:01:26,308 --> 00:01:28,095
and explore its variables.

23
00:01:28,387 --> 00:01:31,015
Text, reference images, or a combination

24
00:01:31,015 --> 00:01:33,639
of both can guide the creation process.

25
00:01:45,047 --> 00:01:49,291
Remix lets you reshape a template with a simple instruction.

26
00:01:49,348 --> 00:01:52,127
Here, a fantasy scene gains a camera view,

27
00:01:52,127 --> 00:01:55,815
with a wide shot, a close-up, and a symmetrical corridor.

28
00:01:55,835 --> 00:01:58,432
The existing structure stays intact

29
00:01:58,432 --> 00:02:02,217
and becomes the starting point for a new variation.

30
00:02:02,403 --> 00:02:04,648
Reference images can guide the change too.

31
00:02:19,883 --> 00:02:22,559
Story mode expands a narrative concept

32
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:25,026
into a sequence of distinct shots.

33
00:02:25,227 --> 00:02:27,727
Set the number of beats and their duration,

34
00:02:27,727 --> 00:02:30,397
then suggest the framing you want to include.

35
00:02:30,724 --> 00:02:35,102
Shared character and world details help the sequence stay connected,

36
00:02:35,102 --> 00:02:38,116
while each beat has its own action and composition.

37
00:02:50,776 --> 00:02:53,813
The p5.js generator turns a visual idea

38
00:02:53,813 --> 00:02:57,729
into an animated sketch with adjustable variables.

39
00:02:58,029 --> 00:03:01,346
Describe the movement, palette, and structure you want,

40
00:03:01,346 --> 00:03:03,493
then run the result in the live viewer.

41
00:03:04,004 --> 00:03:07,866
The built-in library also offers ready-made systems to explore.

42
00:03:08,098 --> 00:03:11,094
Change the controls and watch the artwork respond.

43
00:03:29,862 --> 00:03:32,162
Workflow mode uses a reference image

44
00:03:32,162 --> 00:03:34,945
to choose values from an existing template.

45
00:03:35,067 --> 00:03:37,207
Load the template, add the image,

46
00:03:37,207 --> 00:03:40,815
and describe what matters most, such as palette or mood.

47
00:03:41,004 --> 00:03:42,916
The preview explains the suggested

48
00:03:42,916 --> 00:03:44,888
selections before you import them.

49
00:03:44,991 --> 00:03:47,349
It is a way to connect visual inspiration

50
00:03:47,349 --> 00:03:49,275
with structured prompt controls.

51
00:04:03,607 --> 00:04:05,614
Style Transfer is a workflow

52
00:04:05,614 --> 00:04:08,688
with fifty-three built-in artistic presets.

53
00:04:08,799 --> 00:04:12,213
Describe a subject, then choose a look from the menu,

54
00:04:12,213 --> 00:04:14,878
from oil painting to art nouveau.

55
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:17,160
The workflow generates the image,

56
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:20,380
analyses it, and can refine the result for quality.

57
00:04:20,734 --> 00:04:22,105
Change the preset,

58
00:04:22,105 --> 00:04:25,562
and the same subject takes on an entirely new style.

59
00:04:37,003 --> 00:04:40,526
Image Studio can work on one prompt or a whole batch.

60
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:43,327
Enter one prompt per line, choose the image

61
00:04:43,327 --> 00:04:46,041
model and aspect ratio, and start the run.

62
00:04:46,415 --> 00:04:48,801
Results collect in a gallery as they arrive.

63
00:04:49,131 --> 00:04:51,603
Reference images and optional prompt enhancement

64
00:04:51,603 --> 00:04:53,839
offer additional ways to guide the series.

65
00:05:08,148 --> 00:05:12,265
Video Studio brings motion into the same creative process.

66
00:05:12,338 --> 00:05:14,708
Standard mode supports individual shots,

67
00:05:14,708 --> 00:05:18,545
while Batch mode accepts a list of prompts or a folder of images.

68
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:21,436
Choose the model, duration, and aspect ratio,

69
00:05:21,436 --> 00:05:23,724
then follow the generation progress.

70
00:05:23,923 --> 00:05:25,731
Story and thematic tools provide

71
00:05:25,731 --> 00:05:27,917
another route for connected sequences.

72
00:05:42,576 --> 00:05:46,550
Workflows chain several creative steps into one recipe.

73
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:48,831
This one generates a draft image,

74
00:05:48,831 --> 00:05:52,558
analyses it to extract a rich description, then regenerates

75
00:05:52,558 --> 00:05:55,534
from that enriched prompt for higher quality.

76
00:05:55,688 --> 00:05:57,512
Fill in a prompt, an aspect ratio,

77
00:05:57,512 --> 00:05:59,245
and what to avoid, then run it.

78
00:05:59,312 --> 00:06:01,565
When it finishes, both the draft

79
00:06:01,565 --> 00:06:04,478
and the final image are ready to compare.

80
00:06:23,774 --> 00:06:25,515
Agents begin with a description.

81
00:06:25,689 --> 00:06:28,371
Type a sentence about the character you want,

82
00:06:28,371 --> 00:06:31,335
and the Agent Studio drafts a name, a bio template,

83
00:06:31,335 --> 00:06:33,336
and variables that become knobs.

84
00:06:33,683 --> 00:06:36,548
Tune the personality live, try a test message,

85
00:06:36,548 --> 00:06:40,118
then save the profile to your library or add it straight to a session.

86
00:06:54,780 --> 00:06:57,815
The chat room puts several agents into one conversation,

87
00:06:57,815 --> 00:07:00,648
and every visitor gets a private room of their own.

88
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:04,633
Load a panel, set a shared goal, and start the discussion.

89
00:07:04,854 --> 00:07:07,299
Drop in a reference image part way through

90
00:07:07,299 --> 00:07:10,515
and the agents keep it in view, while older messages fold

91
00:07:10,515 --> 00:07:13,464
into running notes so long sessions stay coherent.

92
00:07:13,621 --> 00:07:14,991
Step in whenever you like,

93
00:07:14,991 --> 00:07:17,538
or stop the exchange when you have what you need.

94
00:07:38,855 --> 00:07:43,263
Glitcher turns a source image into material for experimentation.

95
00:07:43,434 --> 00:07:46,030
Adjust colour and filter controls,

96
00:07:46,030 --> 00:07:51,078
then explore pixel effects that shift, slice, or distort the image.

97
00:07:51,235 --> 00:07:54,395
Draw a selection and the effect applies only

98
00:07:54,395 --> 00:07:57,151
inside it, so small changes add texture

99
00:07:57,151 --> 00:08:00,785
while stronger settings transform the composition.

100
00:08:01,038 --> 00:08:04,198
Compare against the original at any moment.

101
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,328
Press F for focus mode,

102
00:08:06,328 --> 00:08:09,833
which hides every panel so only your image remains.

103
00:08:16,399 --> 00:08:19,984
The Commons turns any screen into a shared canvas.

104
00:08:20,139 --> 00:08:22,995
The host makes a room, picks a piece from the library,

105
00:08:22,995 --> 00:08:24,386
and puts it on the wall.

106
00:08:24,748 --> 00:08:27,623
Everyone who scans the code gets a phone control,

107
00:08:27,623 --> 00:08:30,051
and their choices reshape the wall live.

108
00:08:30,424 --> 00:08:33,235
Ready-made pieces are free, and the host can also

109
00:08:33,235 --> 00:08:36,051
generate a brand new piece from a single prompt.

110
00:08:50,259 --> 00:08:54,144
That is the Synthograsizer: templates, studios,

111
00:08:54,144 --> 00:08:55,898
workflows, agents, glitch art,

112
00:08:55,898 --> 00:09:00,200
and a shared canvas, working together in one place.

113
00:09:00,486 --> 00:09:02,239
Open it up and start playing.
